            "publisher": "National Gallery, London"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "quote",
          "text": "The skull, rendered in anamorphic perspective, another invention of the Early Renaissance, is meant to be a visual puzzle as the viewer must approach the painting from high on the right side, or low on the left side, to see the form as an accurate rendering of a human skull.",
